        <div id="mistakes" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            11. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming Formula 1 Is a High-Protein Shake</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Made with water, a Formula 1 serving has 9 g of protein, about a third of a standard whey scoop. The 17 to 24 g figures on Herbalife's marketing assume nonfat milk or a second powder. Read the per-serving column that matches how you actually mix it before counting it toward your protein goal.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying Formula 3 in the US Expecting Protein</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                In the US, Formula 3 is Cell Activator, a capsule, not a protein powder. The protein add-in is sold as Personalized Protein Powder. A tub labeled Formula 3 Personalised Protein Powder is an import made for another country, with that market's label and possibly a different formula.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Trusting an Amazon Listing Because the Brand Is Real</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Herbalife does not authorize any Amazon sales, so every listing is a third-party reseller. The tub could be old, heat-stored, imported or counterfeit, and Herbalife's refund policy will not cover it. If you want Herbalife, buy through Herbalife's site or a distributor's Herbalife-hosted store.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Treating the Herbalife24 NSF Badge as Brand-Wide</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                NSF Certified for Sport covers specific Herbalife24 products, such as Formula 1 Sport, Rebuild Strength and Enhanced Protein Powder. It does not cover the regular Formula 1 shake, Protein Drink Mix or Personalized Protein Powder. Drug-tested athletes should check the exact product in NSF's database.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Ignoring the Monthly Cost of the Full Plan</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A Formula 1 shake plus Protein Drink Mix costs about $5.49 at Herbalife's retail prices. Two a day is roughly $330 a month before the tea, aloe and supplements distributors often add. Price the whole plan, and ask what discount applies, before committing to an ongoing order.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

