        <div id="faq" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            12. Frequently Asked Questions
          </h2>

          <div class="faq-list">
            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is Herbalife third-party tested?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Only part of the range. Herbalife says Herbalife24 Formula 1 Sport, Rebuild Strength and Enhanced Protein Powder are NSF Certified for Sport, and NSF's database lists them. We found no independent certification for the regular Formula 1 shake, Protein Drink Mix or Personalized Protein Powder, whose US pages mention no NSF, Informed Sport or similar seal. Herbalife describes in-house quality testing for those products.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>How much protein is in Herbalife Personalized Protein Powder?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Each level tablespoon (6 g) gives 5 g of protein and 20 calories, per Herbalife's US label at the time of writing, with 60 servings in the 360 g canister. Herbalife suggests women add up to 2 tablespoons (10 g of protein) and men up to 3 tablespoons (15 g) to each Formula 1 shake. Reaching 25 g of protein takes five tablespoons.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is Herbalife healthy or clean?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  It depends on the product. The Personalized Protein Powder has a short, unsweetened label of soy isolate and whey concentrate. Formula 1 is a fortified shake with 21 vitamins and minerals but also 8 g of added sugar, mostly fructose, plus gums and carrageenan. It can fit a calorie-controlled diet, but it is a processed, sweetened shake rather than a clean-label product.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Does Herbalife contain soy?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Yes. Soy protein isolate is the first ingredient in Formula 1, the Personalized Protein Powder and the Protein Drink Mix, per Herbalife's US labels, and all three also contain milk. Anyone with a soy or milk allergy should avoid them. Herbalife24 Enhanced Protein Powder is milk-based but lists soy lecithin, so it is not soy-free either.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Which Herbalife Formula 1 flavor is best?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Buyers most often name Cookies 'n Cream, French Vanilla and Dutch Chocolate as favorites in retail reviews and distributor feedback, and French Vanilla is a common pick for blending with fruit. We have not tasted them. Note that Herbalife says Cookies 'n Cream and Mint Chocolate are the two flavors that are not gluten-free.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>What are the most common complaints about Herbalife?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Buyers most often complain about price, the low protein in a shake made with water, the added sugar, and distributor pressure to buy bundles or sign up for ongoing orders. People who avoid soy dislike the soy base. Buyers who ordered through Amazon resellers add complaints about short best-by dates and packaging that did not match what they expected.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Can you mix Herbalife Formula 1 with the protein powder?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Yes, that is how Herbalife designs them. Add 1 to 3 tablespoons of Personalized Protein Powder, or 2 scoops of Protein Drink Mix, to a Formula 1 serving. Herbalife says Protein Drink Mix with water brings the shake to 24 g of protein. Three tablespoons of Personalized Protein Powder with water gives about the same, 24 g in total.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

